  "invariants": [
    "Recovery never bypasses a target workflow's own workload/cost admission, authority gates, kill switches, or concurrency controls.",
    "A queued or in-progress target is never duplicated.",
    "Only a trusted event for the exact workflow file on the default branch can prove target liveness.",
    "A recent completed run suppresses recovery even when scheduled delivery is delayed.",
    "A failed/cancelled target may be retried only after the configured failure retry age.",
    "Workload-controlled targets are previewed against workload_control/WORKLOAD_POLICY.json before dispatch.",
    "Paid-ledger wrapper targets are previewed against their bounded cost-wrapper admission before dispatch.",
    "A paid hard stop does not suppress recovery of non-paid workload targets.",
    "At most two workflow_dispatch calls may be emitted per watchdog cycle."
  ]
}
